# Firmware for Meizu 20 (m2381, SM8550 / kalama). Flash a pmOS image and
# every loadable blob is on disk - no manual /lib/firmware top-ups.
#
# Tarball layout (lib/firmware/...), assembled 2026-10-02 from the two
# verified sources (md5-checked on device the same day):
#   qcom/   <- vendor-fw-harvest mainline tree (meizu20_linux):
#              GPU a740_sqe/zap + gmu, adsp/cdsp/modem split fw (DTS paths
#              qcom/sm8550/meizu/*), ipa, vpu. VPU note (2026-10-04 prep
#              round): vpu30_4v.mbn IS the stock firmware (sha256 46c1d9e3,
#              byte-identical to the H3-day on-device pull); the iris driver
#              defaults to a "vpu30_p4.mbn" name that stock never ships, so
#              the bridge is board-DTS firmware-name on &iris (fork commit
#              02e305cf) - never rename files here.
#   ath12k/ <- silime meizu-20-inf-firmware (mainline naming; the set the
#              现网5G verified days ran): WCN7850 hw2.0 amss/board-2/m3
#              (ee2f1a64/89416473/88c1590d) + ncm865.
#   qca/    <- vendor-fw-harvest mainline tree: hmtbtfw20.tlv (26d7ca70)
#              + hmtnv20.* NVRAM family for the WCN7850 BT side.
#   cirrus/ <- audio device day 2026-10-04 (T4c PASS) + r3 (2026-10-05):
#              cs35l45-dsp1-spk-prot wmfw/bin (stock spk tuning renamed to
#              mainline cs_dsp standard; wmfw md5 6d1234f4 = stock harvest
#              anchor; T4c playback verified on device) PLUS per-amp pairs
#              cs35l45-{spk,rcv}-dsp1-spk-prot.* harvested 2026-10-01 from
#              THIS device's stock vendor image (stock-day vendor-fw-cs35l45
#              8-piece set; wmfw all 6d1234f4, spk bin c3b4d6ea, rcv bin
#              5700b016). Kernel fork b52b99bfc6de folds sound-name-prefix
#              into the wm_adsp part string, so @31 (SPK) requests
#              cs35l45-spk-* and @30 (RCV) requests cs35l45-rcv-*; the
#              generic pair stays for the no-prefix fallback. cali/diag
#              bins not shipped: mainline flow (fw=9 spk-prot) never
#              requests them; revisit with Amplifier Mode work.
#              WARNING: the meizu20_linux pro20-dump-extracts firmware set
#              is from a Meizu 20 PRO (M2391) GitHub dump - different
#              device, prot bin md5s differ (86ab6add/13b8f955); never
#              mix it in here.
# Userspace DSP files (silime hexagonfs/, /usr/share/qcom) deliberately
# NOT shipped: never verified on this device - revisit with the SPF
# audio front, don't grow the known-good baseline blind.
# regulatory.db comes from wireless-regdb (base image already has it).
maintainer="ri <ri@example.com>"
pkgname=firmware-meizu-meizu20
pkgver=1
pkgrel=3
pkgdesc="Firmware for Meizu 20 (meizu_20_CN, SM8550 / kalama)"
url="https://postmarketos.org"
arch="aarch64"
license="proprietary"
options="!check !strip !archcheck !tracedeps pmb:cross-native"

source="
	firmware-meizu-meizu20.tar.gz
"

package() {
	mkdir -p "$pkgdir"
	cp -a "$srcdir"/lib "$pkgdir"/
}

sha512sums="
b0d26deb83f77eab8495d3dc02c1e031d078444eaf33b22fcaec4eceff38764aa518cf9d49c21060fc36f7d7397f1a9a43c4589ca0639c1b57b0f48133efe809  firmware-meizu-meizu20.tar.gz
"
